     HTML <header> ELEMENT
     
     The <header> element represents introductory content
     for a page or a section.

     It usually contains:
     • Logo or site title
     • Navigation (navbar)
     • Headings
     • Search bar or icons

     IMPORTANT POINTS:
     • <header> is a semantic element (meaningful to browsers)
     • It improves accessibility and SEO
     • A page can have multiple <header> elements
     • <header> should NOT contain main page content
     • <header> cannot contain another <header>, <footer>,
       or <main> element

     COMMON USAGE:
     • Top section of a webpage
     • Section header inside <section> or <article>

